.TH SISTA 3 "" "Sista" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
sista \- terminal building blocks for C++ applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sista/sista.hpp>
.PP
.B c++ program.cpp \-lSista
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Sista
is a C++17 library for terminal games and animations.
It provides ANSI styling and cursor control together with coordinates,
borders, fields, and movable pawns.
.PP
The umbrella header
.B <sista/sista.hpp>
includes the complete C++ interface.
Individual component headers may be included when preferred.
.PP
This manual describes stable concepts and common usage.
The installed headers and the online API reference are authoritative for
individual declarations.
.SH COMPONENTS
.TP
.BR sista-ansi (3)
Terminal colors, attributes, screen control, and cursor movement.
.TP
.BR sista-field (3)
Fields, coordinates, borders, pawns, and deferred swaps.
.TP
.BR sista-c-api (3)
The opaque-handle C interface provided by
.BR <sista/api.h> .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <iostream>
#include <sista/sista.hpp>

int main()
{
    sista::setForegroundColor(sista::ForegroundColor::GREEN);
    std::cout << "Sista";
    sista::resetAnsi();
    std::cout << '\en';
}
.fi
.PP
Compile the example with:
.PP
.nf
c++ example.cpp \-lSista
.fi
.SH NOTES
The static archive contains Sista code only.
Linking it does not request a fully static C++ runtime or C library.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sista-ansi (3),
.BR sista-c-api (3),
.BR sista-field (3)
